From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:19:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: describe the MT6631 Wi-Fi HIF
 (wifi@180f0000)

wlan_drv_gen3.ko matches "mediatek,wifi" and binds its AHB platform
driver (os/linux/hif/ahb_sdioLike/ahb.c, MtkAhbPltmDriver) to that node.
Without it HifAhbPDev stays NULL, and the first wlanProbe() we triggered
died at glSetHifInfo+0x60 with an Oops: it dereferences
&HifAhbPDev->dev, i.e. a pointer into a NULL struct.

The windows are the ones the stock DTB and the Titan ALPS tree use, in
the order the driver of_iomap()s them: WFDMA 0x180f0000, CQDMA
0x10212180, INFRACFG_AO 0x10001000, CONN remap 0x180e0000; IRQ 290
(WFDMA) and 118 (CQDMA); hardware-values carry the expected chip id
0x788 and the firmware start/end markers 0xa5800. Only the wifi-dma
gate (infracfg CLK_INFRA_CQ_DMA) is listed - mainline has no "conn"
clock provider, the CONSYS power domain is walked through SPM instead.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index f95ee2704..087bc594d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -803,6 +803,37 @@ consys: consys@18070000 {
 		memory-region = <&consys_reserve_memory>;
 		status = "okay";
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Wi-Fi HIF of the same combo chip (WFDMA over AHB).
+	 *
+	 * wlan_drv_gen3.ko matches this node with "mediatek,wifi" and binds its
+	 * AHB platform driver to it (os/linux/hif/ahb_sdioLike/ahb.c,
+	 * MtkAhbPltmDriver). Without the node the driver's HifAhbPDev stays NULL
+	 * and wlanProbe() dereferences a bogus device pointer (glSetHifInfo
+	 * Oops), which is exactly what happened before this node existed.
+	 *
+	 * reg windows, in the order the driver of_iomap()s them:
+	 *   0 0x180f0000  WFDMA (HIF registers, the "SDIO function 1" block)
+	 *   1 0x10212180  CQDMA (command queue DMA, driven by the wifi-dma gate)
+	 *   2 0x10001000  INFRACFG_AO
+	 *   3 0x180e0000  CONN remap config
+	 * IRQ 290 = WFDMA, 118 = CQDMA. Values are the stock ones
+	 * (refs/stock-mt6771.dts) and match the Titan ALPS tree.
+	 */
+	wifi: wifi@180f0000 {
+		compatible = "mediatek,wifi";
+		reg = <0 0x180f0000 0 0x1100>,
+		      <0 0x10212180 0 0x6c>,
+		      <0 0x10001000 0 0x1000>,
+		      <0 0x180e0000 0 0x70>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 290 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>,
+			     <GIC_SPI 118 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		clocks = <&infracfg CLK_INFRA_CQ_DMA>;
+		clock-names = "wifi-dma";
+		hardware-values = <0x788 0xa5800 0xa5800>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
 };
 
